jin: Morning team  I've opened a compact playbook PR that focuses on 429s vs context-limit errors and adds a tiny decision flow for support: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4991

elena: Saw it. Can we make the first-line checklist extremely short for support? Something like: 1) check code+headers, 2) look at token histogram, 3) follow the decision table.

jin: Yep, that's what I pushed. The decision table (condensed) in the PR: 
- status=429 + Retry-After -> honor Retry-After, backoff with jitter, surface to product if recurring
- status=413/400 -> prompt too large: suggest trimming or use a model with larger context
- partial/streamed truncation -> check proxy/nginx timeouts and gateway upstream timeouts

priya: For SDK snippets please reference the canonical ones in /snippets instead of inlining. Support likes one short inline example though. I added a curl and a ~6-line JS snippet that respects Retry-After.

snippets-bot: New snippet PR detected: redwood/snippets#130  contains `retry-after-aware.js` and `retry-after-aware.py`. Link added to docs PR.

elena: Can you paste the JS here? I want to make sure it's non-blocking for browsers.

jin: JS (keeps it compact):
```
async function generateWithRetry(req) {
  for (let attempt=0; attempt<4; attempt++) {
    const res = await redwood.generate(req);
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    const ra = res.headers['retry-after'];
    const delay = ra ? parseInt(ra,10)*1000 : Math.min(1000*(2**attempt), 10000);
    await sleep(delay + Math.random()*100);
  }
  throw new Error('rate-limited');
}
```
Notes: prefer server-provided Retry-After over exponential schedule; add jitter to avoid thundering herd.

priya: I'll mirror that in redwood-py and include a micro-example limiting concurrency with a semaphore.

infra: Quick note for the doc: include an infra pointer about routing logs. The routing tag to grep is `x-route-decision`. If support sees repeated 429s with routing to the same variant, it indicates capacity pressure rather than a single client hitting limits.

elena: Good. Also adding a tiny UX blurb: when trimming, show "We shortened your context to fit model limits" vs cryptic error codes. Product likes explicit wording.

jin: I also added a mini-repro harness suggestion (node + wrk) for QA: a Promise.all with 200 concurrent small requests hitting the same route to confirm fallback kicks in. Link to harness snippet in PR body.

priya: CI reminder from me: run `yarn docs:snippets:lint` and `make docs-validate-links` before merging. I fixed one broken anchor in the err-ref that pointed at `#backoff-patterns` (now `#retry-patterns`).

